100	Since these are overload sets that we want to express, the OOPSLA paper suggests adding a type-level 
101	restriction called {\it multiple instantiation exclusion}
102	which outlaws {\tt BadList} by preventing traits and objects from being subtypes of multiple instantiations
103	of a single type.  However, the paper does not further motivate this restriction, nor provide any
104	alternative solutions, nor explain what overloads the restriction allows and why it works.  We supplement
105	the OOPSLA paper by expanding on this exposition to clearly explain why multiple instantiation 
106	exclusion works and is (arguably) the best choice for the Fortress programming language.
